  "text_md": "The distributed middleware architecture of the application was based on the framework described in [10]. The physics of the scene was simulated using the Bullet Physics Library. Simplified forms of non-convex pieces and holes were designed for the physics simulation in order to facilitate their manipulation, as the Bullet Physics Library does not handle non- convex meshes properly.\n\n***Fig. 2.** on Top: six holes complexity task description. On Bottom: two holes complexity task*\n\n*description In both cases, twelve pieces were involved, six ”fitters” to place in the holed box* *and six ”non-fitters” to place in the disposal zone.*\n\nThe virtual coordinates of the flystick were linked to the physical ones by the mean of a standard proportional derivative control scheme for positions and a suboptimal control scheme with a quadratic cost for rotations, as described in [32]. Performance levels were set at\n\nwww.bulletphysics.org\n",
